 "notes": "Ledger grid is on the RIGHT page (p.125); printed annotations are on the LEFT page (p.124). Running heads \"HOW TO TRADE IN STOCKS\" / \"CHART TWELVE\" and page numbers 124/125 are not transcribed as annotations. Group labels printed on the DATE row: U. S. STEEL, BETHLEHEM STEEL, KEY PRICE.\n\nYear: 1939 (printed above DATE). Chart runs SAT JULY 15 through Aug 25; July 15 1939 confirmed a Saturday. Month rolls from July to August mid-chart (no year change). Trading days Mon-Sat; no Sunday rows.\n\nThe first dated row, \"SAT JULY15\", has no handwritten entries, so it is omitted (only rows with at least one entry are included). Other blank rows (19, 20, 24-Jul, 26-28, SAT29, 31, AUG.1-3, SAT5, 8, SAT12, 14-16, SAT19, 22-Aug, 25-Aug) also omitted.\n\nInk convention holds throughout: UT columns black, DT columns red, all rally/reaction columns (SR/NR/NRC/SRC) blue pencil. Every row where US, BS and KP all appear satisfies KP = US + BS.\n\nUnderline findings (verified by pixel sampling on the source scans):\n- Header carried-forward pivotal points: heavy BLACK single underlines (sampled RGB neutral, R-B ~= -1 to -7).\n- July 25 upward-trend tops (55 1/8 / 65 3/4 / 120 7/8): RED single underlines (R-B ~= 32-38).\n- Aug 24 downward-trend bottoms (41 5/8 / 51 7/8 / 93 1/2): BLACK single underlines. US and KP are clearly black/dark (R-B ~= 2); BS 51 7/8 underline is fainter (brighter, R-B ~= 8, near neutral) \u2014 read as black to match rowmates and the carry-forward convention, but with lower confidence on color.\n\nCorrections made against the low-zoom overview during detailed review: July 21 US = 52 1/2 and KP = 115 1/2 (not 115 1/8); July 18 KP = 113 7/8 (not 113 3/8); Aug 18 BS = 55 1/8 and KP = 100 1/8 (not 5/8). Several auxiliary crop files in the scratchpad (z_bs_bot.png, RB_BS.png, RB_KP.png, crop_kp_bot.png) actually belong to a DIFFERENT/later chart and were disregarded; only c-70-prefixed crops and self-made crops of c-70-RB/RT were trusted.",
